  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more left-skewed (i.e., has a higher concentration of probability on favorable outcomes). To evaluate skewness in this context, we assess how the probabilities are distributed across favorable versus unfavorable outcomes. For Lottery A: 90% chance of 3000€ (favorable) and 10% of 0€ (unfavorable); for Lottery B: 45% chance of 6000€ (favorable) and 55% of 0€ (unfavorable). Lottery A assigns a higher probability mass to a positive outcome (90%) compared to Lottery B (45%), so Lottery A is more left-skewed. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A. The information needed to apply the reason is available in the problem, so the reason can be applied.",
